## Summary

| Severity | Count | Pattern |
|----------|-------|---------|
| 🔴 Critical | 6 | Method called, result discarded, zero assertions |
| 🟠 High | 3 | `Assert.IsNotNull` only — no value checks |
| 🟡 Medium | 4 | Missing negative / edge-case paths |

**Root cause:** Every test follows the same template — call the method, maybe `IsNotNull`, done. This inflates line coverage to 95% while verifying almost nothing. A mutation testing tool (e.g., Stryker.NET) would show near-0% mutation kill rate, which is the real measure of test quality here.
